A||||4||My7Fieros||Some "decent" things or whatever, that came out of this.....||||1||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||09-12-2001||07:06 PM||||Hard to say, but what I mean is the "positive" aspects of Americans throughout this ordeal.<BR> <BR>No problems or mentions of any kind of race relation problems...ALL Americans come together when in crisis.<P>People and politicians put aside their political differences and support the President...Repulicans and Democrats, Conservatives and Liberals all stand behind the President....once again, ALL Americans.<P>Foreign nations advising of thier condolenses and offering of help (even Russia and China &lt;!&gt; ).<P>The state of Mississippi declared a "state of emergency" there....reason because during a state of emergency in MS, you CANNOT raise gas prices! (and its working)<P>The Governor of Arkansas advises everyone that has been the victim of gas price hikes to keep their receipts...for an upcomming class action lawsuits. Tennessee has not risin its gas prices (maybe very slightly).<P>Last but not least is the incredible generosity of ALL Americans, especially New Yorkers.....did you see all the people lining up to give blood.<P>Its amazing what the people of this nation will do in time of crisis...if we could always be like this......................<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_3.gif">  <P><BR>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><P><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||09-12-2001||07:17 PM||||Well said.  Who knows...maybe our country will be like this now.  This could change a lot of things.  It is amazing to see how many people are willing to help.  Here a local raido station is doing a red cross donation drive to get money.  I am gonna have to find my spare change and head out there.  Take care!<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||09-12-2001||07:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B><BR> <BR>No problems or mentions of any kind of race relation problems...ALL Americans come together when in crisis.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Except against people of Arab descent....<P>But I do agree, it is nice to see people band together in times of crisis, and put all differences aside.  Hopefully this good faith can carry on beyond this tragedy.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||09-12-2001||07:44 PM||||A quote from the movie "Star Man" come to mind after reading this post.  The Alien in the movie stated "You know what I find fascinating about you Species? You are at your best when things are at their worst."<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_4.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||09-12-2001||08:38 PM||||A radio station did a drive for the local Red Cross chapter today. They raised over $25,000 in less than 8 hours. I found that to be truly amazing.<P>One news channel also stated that there were no reports of looting or anything like that in the city. They did say that the people who were there and didn't have families to go home to, were staying to help in any way they could.<P>I did see three car accidents today, it seems peoples minds were not on their driving.<P>update: There has been over $80,000 donated to the Lehigh Valley chapter of the American Red Cross disaster relief fund within the past two days.<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
